      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Stop doesn't mean changing who you are overnight—it means slowly dropping the weight of the performance, piece by piece, until the mask feels too heavy to bother with. You don't have to announce it to anyone; just start letting your real reactions, your real silences, your real apathy show in small, careless moments. The identity you're failing at isn't yours—it's a costume you were handed, and you're allowed to take it off, even if it means standing there in nothing but your own hollow truth. And if that truth feels empty right now, that's okay—emptiness is just the room you make for something real to finally end up in.",
